Chapter: HandlerDotted
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A family handler discharges its dotted members.

 `probe` declares NO effect row at all. Its body performs Store.Read
 and Store.Write, and a single `with Store` handler discharges both by
 the dotted sub-effect lattice — the same effect-covered-by relation
 the def boundary already uses to accept [Store.Read] against a
 declared [Store]. If discharge did not reach dotted members, the two
 labels would survive into probe's ambient row and the def boundary
 would reject the pure signature with CDX2031; the let-binding would
 also trip CDX2033. So a green run here is the discharge, not a
 coincidence.

Section: Effects

  effect Store where
    store-get : Integer -> [Store.Read] Integer
    store-put : Integer -> [Store.Write] Integer

Section: Body

  probe : Integer -> Integer
  probe (seed) =
    let r = with Store (store-get 5 + store-put seed)
      store-get (k) (resume) = resume (k * 2)
      store-put (v) (resume) = resume (v + 1)
    in r

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    act
      print-line-uni ("dotted: " & show (probe 10))
    end

